  "description": "The \u0027object_states_cached\u0027 dataset is designed to track and record the states and outcomes of various project-related objects and their execution processes. It includes detailed information about project keys, object identifiers, job and scenario details, execution steps, and timestamps for start and end times. This dataset is particularly useful for monitoring and analyzing the performance and results of different project scenarios and jobs, providing insights into the success or failure of these processes. It also includes metadata such as warnings count and execution type, which can help in debugging and optimizing project workflows. The dataset is structured to support detailed analysis of project execution, making it valuable for project managers and data analysts who need to ensure efficient and successful project operations. The inclusion of JSON objects in the \u0027result\u0027 column allows for flexible data representation and detailed outcome reporting, enhancing the dataset\u0027s utility in complex project environments.",
